{
  "_comment": [
    "Item attributes: what an item is, beyond its grade. Many per item, for",
    "coins and notes alike -- a coin can be DCAM and First Strike and",
    "CAC-approved, a note a star note and a fancy serial and No Motto.",
    "docs/specs/item-attributes-design.md, section 2.",
    "",
    "attribute_group says what kind of fact each is: serial (read from a",
    "note's serial), variety, release (each service's own pedigree, kept",
    "apart because each defines its own window), verification (CAC) and",
    "qualifier (what a holder says instead of, or beside, a grade).",
    "applies_to limits the editor's offer to coins, notes or either.",
    "",
    "Each keeps the service's own term. 'Star (eye appeal)' is NGC and PMG's",
    "star, not a star note. 'Godless' is the collectors' word for the No",
    "Motto $1 Silver Certificates (Series 1928-1935G).",
    "",
    "reference_alias: other names, as in banknote.json."
  ],
